26. The authority boundary

This canonical schema gives us a very clean boundary:

                    AUTHORITATIVE
                         │
       ┌─────────────────┼─────────────────┐
       │                 │                 │
    Identity          Events           Knowledge
       │                 │                 │
       └─────────────────┼─────────────────┘
                         │
                    Cognition
                         │
                    Planning
                         │
                    Execution
                         │
                         ▼
                       Events

while:

AUTHORITATIVE
     │
     ├────────► Graph
     ├────────► Embeddings
     ├────────► Retrieval indexes
     └────────► Cache

can always be rebuilt.

That is the storage architecture I would want MOS to have.

